+## Agent authorization candidate review
+
+Use `ai.boundary.candidate.inspect` with only `candidate_id` to review a retained candidate.
+The server loads this Hunt's latest observation, resolves its stored evidence references and
+returns a non-executable `boundary-review-proposal/v1` with exact `missing_facts`.
+
+`ready_for_review` means the retained metadata is complete enough for review, not that ownership,
+policy applicability, tool behavior or a vulnerability has been proved. `needs_context` names
+missing facts without ending unrelated authorized work. Neither status authorizes execution.
+
+The capability performs no target traffic, reads no credentials or raw response bodies, and
+returns no prompts or executable contracts. It does not mutate a candidate, queue a scan,
+consume a verification slot, or change the Hunt's authorization. Normal Hunt action/time
+accounting and idempotency still apply. Stored business-policy references are checked against
+approved invariants on the same target; caller prose and source labels are not approval.
+
+The draft `/ai/boundary/hypotheses/compile` and `/ai/boundary/proposals/materialize` REST endpoints
+are not native Hunt capabilities. Do not infer that a Command Arsenal entry is callable through
+`/hunts/{hunt_id}/capabilities`. Match each operation to the actual live schema.
 
